From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] label S9+ RTC metadata nodes for M4 SDHMS

# Reason: On M4-0218 with SELinux Enforcing, SDHMS reports `fstat failed: EACCES` for the exact S9+ RTC date/time/since_epoch nodes at logcat lines 180708, 180710 and 180711. All three remain generic `sysfs`; the existing `sysfs_rtc` type already has system_app file/dir read/getattr/open permissions. A live `chcon` trial returned `Permission denied`, and its trap plus readback confirmed all labels stayed generic.
# Affected: extend the existing M4 vendor-restore policy helper and lock with three exact RTC genfscon rules alongside the two existing backlight rules. Record patch series/hash and docs outside this diff. No allow rule, threshold, brightness scale, kernel, vendor blob, radio or protected partition changes.
# Verify: helper idempotence and all-node duplicate/conflict/missing-permission negatives; stage a copy of the actual vendor CIL and prove exactly three genfscon-only additions; compile the complete split policy with secilc; clean ordered patch replay; final ext4 image readback and fresh Enforcing runtime labels/SDHMS logs.
# Rollback: remove 0218 from series/source lock and rebuild the previous M4-0218 package; remove only the three RTC rules from the helper lock/source.

